# Domains that commonly return 403/429 to automated checkers (bot protection)
# even when the link is fine for a real browser. Excluded to avoid false alarms.
facebook\.com
instagram\.com
linkedin\.com
# Google Maps "search" deep links are generated, not pages that 404; skip them.
google\.com/maps
maps\.google\.com
# The card renderer in index.html builds markup by string concatenation, e.g.
#   '<a href="' + esc(l.href) + '"' ...     '<img ... src="' + img + '"/>'
# lychee --include-verbatim reads the raw source and treats those JS fragments
# as href/src values, reporting them as phantom file:// "not found" errors.
# It opened a fresh issue on every run (60 so far). These are code, not links.
# Patterns match the URL as lychee reports it (space -> %20).
esc\(l\.href\)
%20\+%20img%20\+%20
# Sites that return 403/401 to automated checkers but load fine in a browser.
# Confirmed against the first full cards.json scan (2026-09-14). Listing them
# keeps the report meaningful — without this the weekly run reports 8 "errors"
# that are all healthy, and real breakage hides among them.
do512family\.com
costco\.com
heb\.com
schoolofrock\.com
spectrum\.com
waco-texas\.com
wildflower\.org
homepy\.korean\.net
# bgctx.org drops the TCP connection on CI runners ("connection reset by peer")
# on every attempt, including the site root. The page itself is live — it is
# indexed and reachable from a browser. Nothing about the URL to fix, so ignore
# it rather than leave a permanent red mark in the report.
bgctx\.org
# Second round, 2026-09-14. Each of these was confirmed live and correct by
# search before being listed here; the checker is being told to stop crying
# wolf, not to look away from something broken.
#   themonumentcafe.com   timed out twice at 20s, then 403'd at 30s
#   600degreespizzeria.com  403 to the checker, #1-rated restaurant in town
#   spacecenter.org       Space Center Houston, slow enough to time out
# Note these are flaky rather than consistent: a different subset fails each
# run, which is the signature of rate limiting, not of dead links.
themonumentcafe\.com
600degreespizzeria\.com
spacecenter\.org
